                <pb facs="0628" n="516" sameAs="frus:frus1935v03/pg516"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">701.4193/59: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Johnson</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peiping</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1935-05-28T12:00:00+08:00">May 28, 1935—noon</date>.<lb/>[Received
                        May 28—6:43 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>221. The British Minister, Sir Alexander Cadogan, has received word that his
                    credentials as Ambassador are being forwarded to him via Siberia. His present
                    plans contemplate trip to Chungkiang [<hi rendition="#italic">Chungking?</hi>]
                    thence to Nanking arriving there latter part of June at which time he will
                    present his credentials. Pending formal presentation of credentials the status
                    of mission here will remain a legation.</p>
                <closer>For the Minister:<lb/><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                        >Lockhart</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
